{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_eupqiqhw3buui3wh3evxlujynxnlm3kaebqogaksotgqcgtwsvya","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **The Rust translation matches the C exactly — no divergences found, no fixes to `src/lib.rs` were needed.**\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate item | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo check` compiles | clean, zero warnings (`--all-targets`) |\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — 0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols | ✅ `diff` of `nm -D --defined-only` is **empty**; all Rust undefined syms are libc/libgcc-unwind |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row (24) passes randomized | ✅ 25/25 tests |\n| Binary stdout parity | N/A — `CMakeLists.txt` has no `add_executable`; the `driver` *library* export is compared via fd-1 capture instead |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row (12) has a passing test | ✅ 14/14 tests |\n| Every feature combination | ✅ `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]` → one config; ran both default and `--no-default-features` |\n\n## What was built\n\n- `SYMBOLS.md` / `ERRORS.md` / `CONFIGS.md` — mechanically derived surfaces. The key finding for `ERRORS.md`: the C has **zero** explicit error paths (no `assert`, sentinel, null check or range check), so the rejection surface is entirely implicit — NULL deref, degenerate/negative counts, signed-overflow UB, and the `>=` boundary.\n- `tests/common/mod.rs` — harness. Both `.so`s are `dlopen`ed and only their exported symbols are called. Two non-obvious requirements it handles:\n  - **`static int inner` is per-mapping**, and `dlopen` refcounts by path, so `Pair::fresh()` copies both `.so`s to unique temp paths to get a virgin `inner == 1`.\n  - **Pointer returns aren't directly comparable** (the two libraries' statics live at different addresses), so each call compares a *`RetClass` identity* (`Arg` vs `LibStatic`) plus `*ret` plus `*outer`-after.\n- `tests/phase_b_valid_paths.rs`, `phase_c_error_paths.rs`, `phase_d_symbols.rs`, `run_tests.sh`.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **`--test-threads=1` is mandatory.** `driver` output is captured by redirecting fd 1, which is process-global, so libtest's own progress text leaks into the capture under parallelism — this produced a false \"divergence\" on the first run. The harness now detects foreign bytes and panics with an explicit message rather than reporting a bogus mismatch; `run_tests.sh` sets the flag.\n2. **I mutation-tested the suite** to confirm it isn't vacuous. Flipping `>=`→`>` was caught by 8 tests; `INNER` 1→2, discarding `driver`'s returned pointer, returning `outer` instead of `&inner`, and `wrapping_add`→`saturating_add` were each caught by 24–25. `src/lib.rs` was fully restored afterward and re-verified line-by-line against the C.\n\nNote the crate has no VCS (`git status` → not a repository), so the mutation restore was done by targeted text replacement rather than `git checkout`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":349,"cache_read_input_tokens":86307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":349,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9119c04a-b44e-4315-8895-ef68c21781bb","uuid":"40645e27-a82a-4269-8ea6-ad57584cebb7","timestamp":"2026-09-05T03:03:32.541Z"}
